Face-ism Ratio
Tile ratio of face to body in an image that influences the
way the person in the image is perceived. '


Images depicting a person with a high face-ism ratio-the face takes up most of           I   The term face-ism is used by some
the image-focus attention on the person's intellectual and personality attributes.           researchers to refer to the tendency of the
                                                                                             media to represent men in high face-ism
Images depicting a person in a low face-ism ratio- the body takes up most of the
                                                                                             images, and 'NOmen in low face·ism imagcs-
image- focus attention on the physical and sensual attributes of the person. The             also referred to as txxJy-ism,
face-ism ratio is calculated by dividing the distance from the top of Ihe head to the
bottom of the chin (head height) by the distance from the lop of the head 10 the         ~ The seminal 'NOI'k  on face·ism is MFace-ism ~
lowest visible part of the txxJy (total visible height). An image without a face would       by Dane Archer, Debra D. Kimes, and MIChael
have a face-ism ratio of 0.00, and an image with only a face would have a face-              Barrios, PsydJOlqfy Tooay, 1978, p. 65-66;
ism ratio of 1.00. Irrespective of gender, people rate individuals in high face-ism          and - Face-ism: 5 StudIeS of Sex·Dlfferences in
