A Fibonacci sequence is a sequence of numbers in which each number is the             , The seminal work on the Fibonacci sequence
sum af the two preceding numbers (e.g., 1, 1,2,3,5,8, 13). Patterns exhibiting          is Uber Abaci [Book of the Abacus] by
                                                                                          Leona rdo of Pisa, 1202. Contemporary seminal
the sequence are commonly found in natural forms, such as the petals of flowers,
                                                                                          works include The Geometry of Art and Life by
spirals of galaxies, and bones in the human hand. The ubiquity of the sequence in         Matila Ghyka, Dover Publications, 1978
nature has led many to conclude that patterns based on the Fibonacci sequence             [19461; Elements of Dynamic Symmetry by Jay
