Usability needs have to do with how easy and forgiving a design is to use. For
example, configuring a video recorder to record programs at a later time should be                                                                                                                                  Usability
easily accomplished , and the recorder should be tolerant of mistakes. If the diffi·
cully of use is too great. or the consequences of simple errors too severe, usability
                                                                                                                                                                                 PhYSIological
needs are not satisfied. Designs at this level are perceived to be of moderate value.
