the best choice. For example. in a consumer study, people participating in a taste-                                                             rnes
test rated a known brand of peanut butter as superior to two unknown brands,                                                                    mbl                     !II

even though one of the unknown brands was objectively better, as determined by                                                                  mkstl:
earlier blind taste tests. Recognition of an option is often a sufficient condition for                                                         more
making a choice. 2                                                                                                                              mv
