Storytel Iing
A method of crea li ng imagery, emotiorls, and understand-
ing of events through an interaction be tween a storyteller
and an audience .


Storytelling is uniquely human. It is the original method of passing knowledge from      1   The seminal work on storyte lling is Aristotl e's
one generation to the next, and remains one of the most compelling methods                   Poetics. Additional seminal references include,
for richly communicating knowledge . Storytelling can be ora l, as in the trad itional       The Hero with a Thousand Faces by Joseph
                                                                                             Campbell, Princeton University Press, 1960;
telling of a tale; visua l, as in an information graph or movie; or textual, as in a
                                                                                             ;md How to Tell a Story; and Other Essays
poem or novel. More recently, digital storytelling has emerged, which involves               by Mark Twain, Oxford University Press, 1996.
telling a story uSing digital media . This might take the form of a computerized slide       A nice contemporary reference on visual
show, a digital video, or educational software. A storyteller can be any instrument of       storytelling is Graphic Storytelling by Will Eisner,
information presentation that engages an audience to experience a set of events. j           Poorhouse Press, 1996.



Good storytelling experiences generally require certain fu ndamental elements.
While additional elements can be added to further augment the quality of a story
or storytelling experience, they can rarely be subtracted without detriment. The
fundamental elements are:

        Setting- The setting orients the audience, providing a sense of time and
        place for the story.

        Characters- Character identification is how the audience becomes
        involved in the story, and how the story becomes relevan t.

        Plot- The plot ties events in the story together, and is the channel through
        wh ich the story can flow.

        Invisibility- The awareness of the storyteller fades as the audience focuses
        on a good story. When engaged in a good movie or book, the existence of
        the medium is forgotten .

        Mood- Music, lighting, and style of prose create the emotiona l tone of
                                                                                                                                                    Black Gra nite
        the story.                                                                                                                                  Flowing Water

        Movement- In a good story, the sequence and flow of events is clea r and                                                                                                 Asymmetric Table
        interesting. The storyline doesn't stall.
                                                                                                                                                           _---- z-.:::::s::::...:::::..-·c;:·::-~   \I
                                                                                                                                                     ~--
Use storytelling to engage an audience in a design , evoke a specific emotional
response, or provide a rich context to enhance learning. When successfully
employed, an audience will experience and recall the events of the story in a personal
way- it becomes a part of them . This is a phenomenon uniq ue to storytelling.

See also Framing, Immersion, and Wayfind ing.




