The top-down lighting bias can also influence the perception of the naturalness or
unnaturalness of familiar objects. Objects that are depicted with top-down lighting                                                                                                                                                                                       The Circles hi from above appear
look natural, whereas familiar objects that are depicted with bottom-up ligh ting look                                                                                                                                                                                    convex. whereas tile Circles lit tram
